  "permittedCallOrder": [
    "A-owned Swift lease and runtime pass preflight; owned task validates the lease and calls IO.",
    "Apple IO enqueues the direct Lib byte method on the global queue and suspends; no native account lease has been acquired.",
    "An AccountSelect/Stop transition retires A Swift leases and obtains native application writer lock; selection of B can complete before the queued call starts.",
    "The queued old request enters Lib; native pinkhaTorahScope now acquires B current-app read lock and derives B signer.",
    "If B is authorized for that same shared Space and other operation preconditions hold, native can commit under B. Swift original-owner/claim checks can withhold the response but cannot prevent that commit."
  ],
  "requiredOwnerClosure": [
    "Supply an atomic handoff/fence linking the queued operation to the original owned native account lifetime, or identify and qualify an already-existing serialization guarantee covering the complete queue-wait/account-transition boundary.",
    "Preserve all native current ACL/source/target/signer validation. An expected identity or lease token may reject a stale owner but must never grant authority.",
    "Demonstrate that a queued old-account mutation cannot enter under a replacement account; after an original-account handoff, retain original durable-ACK and drain behavior.",
    "A separate final Swift recheck before calling Lib or postflight reply rejection is insufficient unless the account transition and native entry are atomically serialized."
  ],
